  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CARE-DRC Tuma+ Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The TUMA+ consortium, consisting of six core partners, namely CARE Nederland, CARE DRC, ADJ, SARCAF, PARDE and HE, will cover 9 health zones in North and South Kivu provinces. The consortium will seek to increase the coverage of sexual and reproductive health services and reduce gender-based violence (GBV) for the improved well-being of women and youth (the Specific Objective), directly targeting a total of 356.967 individuals and focusing on youth aged 10-24 and women and men over 25, including internally displaced persons (IDPs), host communities, and/or survivors of sexual violence.</narrative>
  </description>
